                  "text": "15 Extinction Diameter: Pressure Dependence Comparison of predicted and measured de,HF and de,CF as a function of operating pressure for of n-dodecane droplets burning in air. (do = 4.00 mm). • Both hot and cool flame extinction diameter has a non-linear dependence on pressure. • de,CF decreases as pressure is increased, and is absent at 3 atm as the droplet burns to completion following a “Warm” flame combustion • The de,CF is most sensitive to: •O2QnOOH → •OQn`OOH + OH •O2QnOOH → QnOOH + O2"
