          "node": {
            "id": "exp:PSI-117:2c306866dd6b6ea46e3d",
            "type": "Experiment",
            "properties": {
              "title": "Initial-size effects in free-floating n-heptane/iso-octane droplets on the ISS",
              "summary": "The accessed abstract reports ISS experiments and numerical simulations of equi-volume n-heptane/iso-octane droplets with initial diameters from 0.8 mm to below 5 mm. Smaller droplets remain in the hot-flame regime; larger droplets can undergo radiative extinction and cool-flame transition. Measured flame radiance supports radiation as a controlling mechanism. No preferential vaporization was observed for the close-boiling component pair.",
