              "summary": "One-dimensional numerical study of 0.5 mm n-heptane droplets at 1 atm and 298 K. With 5% ozone, the 21% oxygen case sustains a cool flame, while the 10% oxygen case develops increasing oscillations. The reported mechanism couples low-temperature chain branching and propagation/termination with fuel leakage through the flame. These are simulation outputs, not new physical test runs.",
