            "type": "Experiment",
            "properties": {
              "title": "Reduced-gravity n-butanol droplet experiments and numerical comparison",
              "summary": "Cornell drop-tower experiments track n-butanol droplets with initial diameters 0.56–0.57 mm in standard atmosphere under reduced gravity. Video-derived diameter, flame stand-off ratio and burning-rate measurements are compared with transient combustion simulations. The dissertation reports complete burning without flame extinction under the experimental conditions. Model species/reaction counts differ between abstract and methods, so no count is selected here.",
              "keywords": [
