                  "text": "Effect of buoyancy a) Temperature distribution and streamlines, and b) heat release rate, for DME diffusion cool flame with and without buoyancy for identical conditions (XDME= 0.587, UF = 62.3 cm/s, UO = 50.9 cm/s, a ~ 90 s-1, P = 1 atm)  Buoyancy lifts the flame upward.  Without buoyancy, 1D and 2D models predict the flame at or near the stagnation plane due to momentum- balanced BC.  The peak flame temperature in 1D is slightly lower compared to the 2D prediction, but the peak HRR shows the opposite trend.  Temperature gradient is higher in 1D calculation. More diffusive heat loss."
