                  "locator": "page 11",
                  "text": "11 Extinction Diameter Comparison of measured and predicted hot and cool flame extinction diameter for different initial droplet diameter for the three n-alkane fuels (atmospheric air) • High temperature combustion is strongly governed by the small species kinetics – all three fuels share nearly identical values of HF extinction diameter for the same do • The LTC differs with carbon number as each involve reactions associated with the carbon number of the fuel and the large intermediates produced. The overall rates of isomerization of radical-O2 adducts controlling rate of degenerate chain branching rate increase from C7 to C12 • The CF extinction is dictated by the increase in decomposition of •O2QnOOH for all three fuels."
